  "question": {
    "text": "The line $y=m x$ bisects the area enclosed by lines $x$ $=0, \\mathrm{y}=0$ and $\\mathrm{x}=3 / 2$ and the curve $\\mathrm{y}=1+4 \\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{x}^{2}$\r\n\r\nThen the value of $\\mathrm{m}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NKLqg",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{6}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "S35hB",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6HYL9",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EOgER",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y=1+4 x-x^{2}=5-(x-2)^{2}$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/MzY8V4T1MJrhjGUbkQlVjCwugtbohShak5aX8iphZQQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nWe have $\\int_{0}^{3 / 2}\\left(1+4 x-x^{2}\\right) \\mathrm{dx}=2 \\int_{0}^{3 / 2} \\operatorname{mx} \\mathrm{dx}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{3}{2}+2\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)-\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{27}{8}\\right)=\\mathrm{m} \\cdot \\frac{9}{4}$\r\n\r\nOn solving we get $\\mathrm{m}=\\frac{13}{6}$",
    "image": null
  },
